.TH "CSSUNPARSEDVALUE.ENTRIES" "3JS" "August 15, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSUnparsedValue.entries \- CSSUnparsedValue: entries() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]entries()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]CSSUnparsedValue\f[R] interface returns a new \f[I]array
iterator\f[R] that yields \f[CR][index, value]\f[R] pairs for each item
in the object.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
entries()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A new iterable iterator.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Iterating over index/value pairs
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] value = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnparsedValue([\(dq1em\(dq, \(dq#445566\(dq, \(dq\-45px\(dq]);

\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] [index, fragment] \f[B]of\f[R] value.entries()) {
  console.log(index, fragment);
}
\f[I]// 0 \(dq1em\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// 1 \(dq#445566\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// 2 \(dq\-45px\(dq\f[R]
.EE
